  <data name="About.Heading" xml:space="preserve"><value>About the project</value></data>
  <data name="About.What.Heading" xml:space="preserve"><value>What this is</value></data>
  <data name="About.What.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Dev Interview Trainer is a free question bank for developer interviews. Every question has a level from junior to architect, a topic and a type, and comes with a worked answer, an explanation and links to sources. The first stack is .NET. The site is available in Russian and English.</value></data>
  <data name="About.Licence.Heading" xml:space="preserve"><value>Licences</value></data>
  <data name="About.Licence.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The questions are published under CC BY-SA 4.0: you may copy and adapt them, credit the project and share adaptations under the same licence. The source code is published under the MIT licence.</value></data>
  <data name="About.Contribute.Heading" xml:space="preserve"><value>How to contribute</value></data>
  <data name="About.Contribute.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Each question is a plain text file and changes are reviewed like code. To add or correct a question, send a change to the repository. Every question needs both languages and at least one authoritative source.</value></data>
